24 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-009 | Primary-constructor criteria (fit for DI/simple initialization; regular constructor when validation is non-trivial, explicit fields read better, the codebase uses that style, or capture hurts understanding). RUN-009 leaves feature use to a clarity judgment; these criteria fix the choice (oracle EXC-003 lineage).
  s: A service with non-trivial constructor validation written with a primary constructor and an init-time guard that the author judges clear: allowed by RUN-009; M's default asks for a regular constructor.
25 CO RUN-009~ m=MN | 'Do not convert constructors mechanically' is RUN-009's 'do not mechanically modernize working code'.
26 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-009 | Records for value semantics/immutability (many DTOs, genuine Value Objects), classes for identity/mutable lifecycle/inheritance/framework behavior; not every DTO or Domain type becomes a record (EXC-003 lineage).
  s: Making every DTO and entity a record is permitted by all 196 policies; M's default rejects it.
27 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-009,RUN-001 | Keep implementation details non-public unless part of the public API; use sealed to communicate deliberate non-inheritance, not as a speculative JIT optimization (EXC-003 lineage).
  s: Making all helper classes public in an application project is allowed by the oracle; M's default keeps them non-public.
28 CO RUN-009 m=D | Modern features (collection expressions, pattern matching, ...) only when they make code easier to read: RUN-009's 'use modern C# when it improves clarity'.
29 XP m=D c=M rel=RUN-009 | 'var' when the type is obvious or unimportant, explicit type when clearer (EXC-003 lineage; also encoded in .editorconfig).
  s: Using explicit types everywhere in a project without a convention: allowed by RUN-009; M's default prefers var where the type is obvious.
30 XP m=M c=M rel=RUN-009 | Standard .NET naming (PascalCase types/methods/properties/public members, camelCase parameters/locals, meaningful names); private fields follow the repository convention. RUN-009 defers to existing repository conventions, which may differ for public members.
  e: private-field naming follows the repository's established convention
  s: An existing codebase names public constants in UPPER_SNAKE_CASE: RUN-009 says follow that convention; M's rule requires PascalCase public members.
